IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cp6-accounts`

-- Tests of cp6-accounts.l4 (sections 107.1 to 111.1 and 118). Sums and differences are worked by hand beside each assertion.

§ `Tests -- the accounts of Canada`

§§ `Section 107.1: gifts to the Minister`

#ASSERT `s 107.1 — the Minister may acquire the money, securities or other property` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 107.1 — the Minister may acquire the money, securities or other property` FALSE)
-- Inputs: the property is securities or other property; terms were stated.
#ASSERT `s 107.1 — the Minister must dispose of the property subject to the terms on which it was made available` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 107.1 — the Minister must dispose of the property subject to the terms on which it was made available` TRUE FALSE)
-- Money is acquired, not disposed of, under the section.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 107.1 — the Minister must dispose of the property subject to the terms on which it was made available` FALSE TRUE)

§§ `Sections 108(2)(a) and 108.2(2)(a): which account a contribution goes to`

#ASSERT `s 108(2)(a) and 108.2(2)(a) — the account to which a contribution of a tier is credited` `the base tier` EQUALS `the Canada Pension Plan Account`
#ASSERT `s 108(2)(a) and 108.2(2)(a) — the account to which a contribution of a tier is credited` `the first additional tier` EQUALS `the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account`
#ASSERT `s 108(2)(a) and 108.2(2)(a) — the account to which a contribution of a tier is credited` `the second additional tier` EQUALS `the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account`

§§ `Section 108(2) and (3): what is credited and charged`

#ASSERT `s 108(2) — the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `a contribution under subsection 8(1), 9(1) or 10(1), or another amount received on account of the base Canada Pension Plan`
#ASSERT `s 108(2) — the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `an amount required to be credited to the Account under an agreement under subsection 39(1) or 80(1) or a regulation under paragraph 89(1)(j) or subsection 107(3)`
#ASSERT `s 108(2) — the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `money received under section 107.1 on account of the base Canada Pension Plan, or the proceeds of disposing of securities or property so received`
#ASSERT `s 108(2) — the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `an amount charged for the use of resources associated with the administration of the Act in relation to the base Canada Pension Plan`
#ASSERT `s 108(2) — the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `interest or an administrative charge collected in relation to money payable under the Act in relation to the base Canada Pension Plan`
#ASSERT `s 108(2) — the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `an amount received under subsection 56(1) of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 108(2) — the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `any other amount`)

#ASSERT `s 108(3) — the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund and charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `an amount payable under the Act in relation to the base Canada Pension Plan as or on account of benefits or otherwise`
#ASSERT `s 108(3) — the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund and charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `an amount required to be charged to the Account under an agreement under subsection 39(1) or 80(1) or a regulation under paragraph 89(1)(j) or subsection 107(3)`
#ASSERT `s 108(3) — the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund and charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `an amount credited to the Account under paragraph 108(2)(e)`
#ASSERT `s 108(3) — the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund and charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `the costs of administration of the Act in relation to the base Canada Pension Plan, under the authority of Parliament`
#ASSERT `s 108(3) — the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund and charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `an amount required to be charged to the Account under section 57 of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act`
#ASSERT `s 108(3) — the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund and charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `the costs, in relation to the base Canada Pension Plan, of administering Part 5 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act in respect of appeals respecting the Act`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 108(3) — the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund and charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` `any other amount`)

§§ `Section 108(4): the most that may be paid out`

-- Balance 1,000,000 plus (assets 5,000,000 less liabilities 2,000,000 = 3,000,000) = 4,000,000.
#ASSERT `s 108(4) — the most that may be paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under section 108` 1000000 5000000 2000000 EQUALS 4000000
#ASSERT `s 108(4) — a payment may be made out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under section 108` 4000000 1000000 5000000 2000000
#ASSERT NOT (`s 108(4) — a payment may be made out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under section 108` 4000001 1000000 5000000 2000000)
-- Liabilities above assets: balance 500 plus (100 less 300 = minus 200) = 300.
#ASSERT `s 108(4) — the most that may be paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under section 108` 500 100 300 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 108(4) — a payment may be made out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under section 108` 300 500 100 300
#ASSERT NOT (`s 108(4) — a payment may be made out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under section 108` 301 500 100 300)

§§ `Section 108.2(2), (3) and (4): the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account`

#ASSERT `s 108.2(2) — the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `a contribution under subsection 8(1.1) or (1.2), 9(1.1) or (1.2) or 10(1.1) or (1.2), or another amount received on account of the additional Canada Pension Plan`
#ASSERT `s 108.2(2) — the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `an amount required to be credited to the Additional Account under an agreement under subsection 39(1) or 80(1) or a regulation under paragraph 89(1)(j) or subsection 107(3)`
#ASSERT `s 108.2(2) — the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `money received under section 107.1 on account of the additional Canada Pension Plan, or the proceeds of disposing of securities or property so received`
#ASSERT `s 108.2(2) — the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `an amount charged for the use of resources associated with the administration of the Act in relation to the additional Canada Pension Plan`
#ASSERT `s 108.2(2) — the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `interest or an administrative charge collected in relation to money payable under the Act in relation to the additional Canada Pension Plan`
#ASSERT `s 108.2(2) — the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `an amount received under subsection 56(1.1) of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 108.2(2) — the amount is paid into the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `any other amount`)

#ASSERT `s 108.2(3) — the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund and charged to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `an amount payable under the Act in relation to the additional Canada Pension Plan as or on account of benefits or otherwise`
#ASSERT `s 108.2(3) — the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund and charged to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `an amount required to be charged to the Additional Account under an agreement under subsection 39(1) or 80(1) or a regulation under paragraph 89(1)(j) or subsection 107(3)`
#ASSERT `s 108.2(3) — the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund and charged to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `an amount credited to the Additional Account under paragraph 108.2(2)(d)`
#ASSERT `s 108.2(3) — the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund and charged to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `the costs of administration of the Act in relation to the additional Canada Pension Plan, under the authority of Parliament`
#ASSERT `s 108.2(3) — the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund and charged to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `an amount required to be charged to the Additional Account under section 57.1 of the Canada Pension Plan Investment Board Act`
#ASSERT `s 108.2(3) — the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund and charged to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `the costs, in relation to the additional Canada Pension Plan, of administering Part 5 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act in respect of appeals respecting the Act`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 108.2(3) — the amount is paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund and charged to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` `any other amount`)

-- Balance 2,000 plus (assets 9,000 less liabilities 4,500 = 4,500) = 6,500.
#ASSERT `s 108.2(4) — the most that may be paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under section 108.2` 2000 9000 4500 EQUALS 6500
#ASSERT `s 108.2(4) — a payment may be made out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under section 108.2` 6500 2000 9000 4500
#ASSERT NOT (`s 108.2(4) — a payment may be made out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund under section 108.2` 6501 2000 9000 4500)

§§ `Sections 108.1 and 108.3: surplus to the Investment Board, and interest`

-- Credit 1,000, immediate obligations 400: the excess 600 is transferred.
#ASSERT `s 108.1(1) — the amount transferred to the Investment Board` 1000 400 FALSE EQUALS JUST 600
-- No excess: nothing to transfer.
#ASSERT `s 108.1(1) — the amount transferred to the Investment Board` 300 400 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 108.1(1) — the amount transferred to the Investment Board` 400 400 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
-- Not covered: an agreement under section 111.1 provides otherwise.
#ASSERT `s 108.1(1) — the amount transferred to the Investment Board` 1000 400 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 250,000 charged plus 12,000 interest.
#ASSERT `s 108.1(2) — the most the Minister may by notice require the Investment Board to pay into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` 250000 12000 EQUALS 262000
#ASSERT `s 108.1(3) — the Minister of Finance must credit interest to the Canada Pension Plan Account` 1
#ASSERT NOT (`s 108.1(3) — the Minister of Finance must credit interest to the Canada Pension Plan Account` 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 108.1(3) — the Minister of Finance must credit interest to the Canada Pension Plan Account` (0 MINUS 5))

#ASSERT `s 108.3(1) — the amount transferred to the Investment Board` 2500 1000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 1500
#ASSERT `s 108.3(1) — the amount transferred to the Investment Board` 100 1000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 108.3(1) — the amount transferred to the Investment Board` 2500 1000 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 108.3(2) — the most the Minister may by notice require the Investment Board to pay into the Consolidated Revenue Fund` 100 5 EQUALS 105
#ASSERT `s 108.3(3) — the Minister of Finance must credit interest to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` 1
#ASSERT NOT (`s 108.3(3) — the Minister of Finance must credit interest to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` 0)

§§ `Section 110: interest on a shortfall`

-- Paid out 900 against a balance of 600: interest runs on 300.
#ASSERT `s 110(1) — the amount on which interest is charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` 900 600 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 110(1) — the amount on which interest is charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` 500 600 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 110(1) — the amount on which interest is charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` 600 600 EQUALS 0
-- The period begins on the day of payment out and ends on the day the Investment Board pays in; both days are in it.
#ASSERT `s 110(1) — a day is in the period for which interest is charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `s 110(1) — a day is in the period for which interest is charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT `s 110(1) — a day is in the period for which interest is charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 110(1) — a day is in the period for which interest is charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 2 28))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 110(1) — a day is in the period for which interest is charged to the Canada Pension Plan Account` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 31) (YMD 2026 4 1))

#ASSERT `s 110(2) — the amount on which interest is charged to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` 1500 1000 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `s 110(2) — the amount on which interest is charged to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` 800 1000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 110(2) — a day is in the period for which interest is charged to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) (YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 110(2) — a day is in the period for which interest is charged to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 30) (YMD 2026 7 1))

§§ `Section 111.1: agreements between the Minister of Finance and the Investment Board`

-- Inputs: the matter is one referred to in sections 107.1 to 110; the terms are satisfactory to the Minister.
#ASSERT `s 111.1(1) — the Minister of Finance may enter into an agreement with the Investment Board about the matter` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 111.1(1) — the Minister of Finance may enter into an agreement with the Investment Board about the matter` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 111.1(1) — the Minister of Finance may enter into an agreement with the Investment Board about the matter` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 111.1(2) — the Minister of Finance may enter into an agreement with the Investment Board about the matter` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 111.1(2) — the Minister of Finance may enter into an agreement with the Investment Board about the matter` FALSE)

§§ `Section 118: the Crown's contributions as employer`

-- 1,200,000 under 9(1) plus 3,500 under 21(2).
#ASSERT `s 118(1) — the amount charged to the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account` 1200000 3500 EQUALS 1203500
-- 400,000 under 9(1.1) and (1.2) plus 1,000 under 21(2).
#ASSERT `s 118(1.1) — the amount charged to the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account` 400000 1000 EQUALS 401000
-- 750 as employer's contributions under the agreement plus 250 for failing to deduct and remit.
#ASSERT `s 118(2) — the amount charged to the Consolidated Revenue Fund and paid to the appropriate authority in the province` 750 250 EQUALS 1000
-- Nothing owed: nothing charged.
#ASSERT `s 118(1) — the amount charged to the Consolidated Revenue Fund and credited to the Canada Pension Plan Account` 0 0 EQUALS 0
